<title>BRAZIL: Brazil publishes sugar export tax exemption.</title>
<headline>Brazil publishes sugar export tax exemption.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's sugar exporters are now free to ship sugar marked out for export in the 1997/98 crop plan without a 40 percent export tax after the government published the exemption today in its official gazette.</p>
<p>The interministerial despatch, signed by Industry and Commerce Minister Francisco Dornelles and Finance Minister Pedro Malan, removes the tax from a total of 5.39 million tonnes out of a total expected harvest of 13.48 million tonnes.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
